# Selecto Bounded Verification Workbook

This workbook runs the verification entry points shipped by current Selecto,
SelectoUpdato, SelectoComponents, and the PostgreSQL write adapter. Each proof
is exhaustive over its named finite model; none claims to prove arbitrary host
code or an unbounded state space.

## Setup

```elixir
Code.require_file(Path.expand("support/bootstrap.exs", __DIR__))
SelectoLivebooksNotebookBootstrap.install_verification!()
```

## 1) Run the ecosystem safety models

```elixir
reports = %{
  query_scope: Selecto.Verification.QuerySafety.verify(),
  domain_contract: Selecto.Verification.ContractSafety.verify(),
  write_scope: SelectoUpdato.Verification.WriteSafety.verify(),
  action_capability: SelectoUpdato.Verification.ActionSafety.verify(),
  portable_command: SelectoUpdato.Verification.PortableCommandSafety.verify(),
  nested_graph: SelectoUpdato.Verification.NestedGraphSafety.verify(),
  action_visibility: SelectoComponents.Verification.ActionVisibility.verify()
}

Enum.each(reports, fn {name, report} ->
  true = report.proved?

  IO.puts(
    "#{name}: #{report.check_count} checks across #{report.state_count} states " <>
      "(#{report.proof_level})"
  )
end)

updato_checks =
  reports
  |> Map.take([:write_scope, :action_capability, :portable_command, :nested_graph])
  |> Map.values()
  |> Enum.sum_by(& &1.check_count)

640 = updato_checks

Map.new(reports, fn {name, report} ->
  {name,
   Map.take(report, [
     :model,
     :proof_level,
     :state_count,
     :invariant_count,
     :check_count,
     :proved?
   ])}
end)
```

## 2) Produce JSON-ready proof material

Proof reports use portable data and can be persisted by the package Mix tasks:
`mix selecto.verify`, `mix selecto_updato.verify`, and
`mix selecto_components.verify`. This cell demonstrates the same JSON boundary
without writing a file.

```elixir
proof_json =
  reports
  |> Map.new(fn {name, report} -> {to_string(name), report} end)
  |> Jason.encode!(pretty: true)

proof_json
```

The PostgreSQL adapter conformance preview and real transactional rollback
probe live in `selecto_updato_feature_tour.livemd`. Atomic generated-key and
owned-set synchronization probes live in
`selecto_updato_nested_writes_workbook.livemd`. Those notebooks intentionally
install the adapter and open direct Postgrex sessions; this bounded-model
workbook does neither.
